#DESCRIPTION
Absorbing-field boundary-condition test: a tophat EM pulse (Ey/Bz step) seeded
in the interior is absorbed at the x-faces.

The `tophat` testcase seeds a discontinuous Ey=1, Bz=1 EM step in the central
half of the domain with zero macroparticles (pure EM).  The step immediately
splits into a right-going and a left-going pulse that travel toward the +x and
-x faces.  Both x-faces use the ABSORBING (outgoing-characteristic) field BC, so
the pulses leave the domain with minimal reflection and the total EM energy
decays.  With conducting/periodic walls the pulses would reflect and the energy
would persist, so EM-energy decay is the decisive absorber signature.

y and z are thin (fake-2D) and periodic.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-10.0                   xMin
 10.0                   xMax
-0.5                    yMin
 0.5                    yMax
-0.5                    zMin
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
40                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
20                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
T                       solveEM

#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
0.01                    mass        Species 0: electron (background, 0 ppc)
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
1.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: electron background
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
1.0e4                   T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#NORMALIZATION
1.0                     lNormSI
1.0                     uNormSI

#TESTCASE
tophat                  testCase

Absorbing (outgoing-characteristic) field BC on both x-faces.
#BFIELDBOXBOUNDARY
absorb                  BoxBoundaryLo
absorb                  BoxBoundaryHi
periodic                BoxBoundaryLo
periodic                BoxBoundaryHi
periodic                BoxBoundaryLo
periodic                BoxBoundaryHi

Characteristic speed for the absorber (code units; 0 = auto -> light speed c=1).
#ABSORB
0.0                     charSpeed

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.4                     dt

#DISCRETIZATION
0.50                    theta
0.0                     ratioDivC2C

#MONITOR
10                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#DIVE
F                       doCorrectDivE

#RESAMPLING
F                       doReSampling

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii pic       plotString
-1                      dnSavePlot
10.0                    dtSavePlot
-1                      dxSavePlot
Ey Bz Ex Ez Bx By       plotVar

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
40.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
